## Part 2–9
```java
import java.util.Scanner;

public class TripCostAnalyzer {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        final int MINUTES_PER_HOUR = 60;

        Scanner input = new Scanner(System.in);

        System.out.print("Enter trip distance in miles: ");
        double distance = input.nextDouble();

        System.out.print("Enter vehicle miles per gallon: ");
        double milesPerGallon = input.nextDouble();

        System.out.print("Enter fuel price per gallon: ");
        double pricePerGallon = input.nextDouble();

        System.out.print("Enter average driving speed: ");
        double averageSpeed = input.nextDouble();

        System.out.print("Enter number of travelers: ");
        int numberOfTravelers = input.nextInt();

        double gallonsNeeded = distance / milesPerGallon;
        double fuelCost = gallonsNeeded * pricePerGallon;
        double travelHours = distance / averageSpeed;

        int wholeHours = (int) travelHours;
        double fractionalHour = travelHours - wholeHours;
        int remainingMinutes = (int) (fractionalHour * MINUTES_PER_HOUR);

        double costPerTraveler = fuelCost / numberOfTravelers;

        System.out.println("Gallons needed: " + gallonsNeeded);
        System.out.println("Fuel cost: " + fuelCost);
        System.out.println("Travel time: " + travelHours + " hours");
        System.out.println("Estimated driving time: " + wholeHours + " hours and " + remainingMinutes + " minutes");
        System.out.println("Fuel cost per traveler: " + costPerTraveler);

        input.close();
    }
}

Sample Run (distance 360, mpg 30, price 4.50, speed 60, travelers 3):

Gallons needed: 12.0
Fuel cost: 54.0
Travel time: 6.0 hours
Estimated driving time: 6 hours and 0 minutes
Fuel cost per traveler: 18.0
