## Part 12
1) Because both distance and speed are int, Java performs integer division first (350 / 80 = 4, truncated), and only afterward converts that result to a double when assigning it. The decimal part is already gone by the time it's stored.
2) Cast just one of the operands to double before the division happens, so Java performs floating-point division instead of integer division.
